<http://data.silknow.org/object/bd69c070-0ae8-3814-869b-2089a228a372>
        a                   ecrm:E73_Information_Object ;
        rdfs:comment        "June 11 - October 31, 2004" , "Each small black and red block on this white cloth is uniquely patterned with motifs and symbols that are recognizably different from clan to clan. These textiles are woven specifically for wear on certain ceremonial occasions, and even today have an important place in the cultural life of the Angami Naga.\nThe hill country of Nagaland in the far northeast of India has changed significantly over the past hundred  years, and is now far more accessible to visitors than ever in the past. Naga peoples also live over the border in Burma." , "In the Spirit of Miss Lucy" ;
        ecrm:P129_is_about  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9b2f5a85-6eab-3612-815e-3754b30e0def> ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    "Exhibition" ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "In the Spirit of Miss Lucy" , "Each small black and red block on this white cloth is uniquely patterned with motifs and symbols that are recognizably different from clan to clan. These textiles are woven specifically for wear on certain ceremonial occasions, and even today have an important place in the cultural life of the Angami Naga.\nThe hill country of Nagaland in the far northeast of India has changed significantly over the past hundred  years, and is now far more accessible to visitors than ever in the past. Naga peoples also live over the border in Burma." , "June 11 - October 31, 2004" ;
        schema:contentUrl   <https://risdmuseum.org/exhibitions-events/exhibitions/spirit-miss-lucy> .

